<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/legend.png?v=na-precip-20261013-1535" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Precipitation intensity (NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity, dBZ, OBSERVED radar echo): <b>LOWEST 5 Very Light</b> cyan/blue (drizzle, mist) &rarr; <b>Light</b> greens (~20-30: light rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Moderate</b> dark green (~30-40: steady rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Heavy</b> yellow/orange (~40-50: heavy rain) &rarr; <b>Severe</b> red (~50-60: severe storms, hail possible) &rarr; <b>Intense</b> magenta/purple (~60-70: violent storms, large hail) &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 70+ Extreme</b> white (destructive hail, debris). Same dBZ always shows the same color in every season — rain, snow, lake-effect snow, thunderstorms. No echo (no precipitation) stays see-through so the map underneath shows.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT OBSERVATION (NEXRAD + ECCC NA radar, 5-6 min mosaic)</p><p><b>Source:</b> Iowa Environmental Mesonet CONUS NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity (NOAA WSR-88D) inside its domain + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) outside it<br/><a href="https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/current/radar.phtml">https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/current/radar.phtml</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>Extended North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>Precipitation intensity (NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity, dBZ, OBSERVED radar echo): <b>LOWEST 5 Very Light</b> cyan/blue (drizzle, mist) &rarr; <b>Light</b> greens (~20-30: light rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Moderate</b> dark green (~30-40: steady rain/snow) &rarr; <b>Heavy</b> yellow/orange (~40-50: heavy rain) &rarr; <b>Severe</b> red (~50-60: severe storms, hail possible) &rarr; <b>Intense</b> magenta/purple (~60-70: violent storms, large hail) &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 70+ Extreme</b> white (destructive hail, debris). Same dBZ always shows the same color in every season — rain, snow, lake-effect snow, thunderstorms. No echo (no precipitation) stays see-through so the map underneath shows.</p><p><b>Sources:</b> Iowa Environmental Mesonet CONUS NEXRAD N0Q base reflectivity (NOAA WSR-88D) inside its domain + ECCC North American Radar Composite 1km rain (RADAR_1KM_RRAI, mm/h) / snow (RADAR_1KM_RSNO, cm/h) outside it<br><b>Precedence:</b> ECCC (rates -> dBZ via NWS Z=300R^1.4 onto the original N0Q key) wins everywhere its RADAR_COVERAGE_*.INV dynamic coverage is valid, including most of CONUS; IEM N0Q (native rendering, itself the original legend) fills ECCC gaps; 10-px cross-fade on the coverage edge; transparent elsewhere.<br><b>Coverage:</b> Extended North America Coverage<br><b>Cloud underlay:</b> real GOES-19/18 Band-13 infrared satellite texture (IR GOES-19 15:20Z+GOES-18 15:20Z n=2080549)<br></p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_Basin.kml">Great Lakes Basin Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>◉ <b>Extended North America Coverage</b> (this view)<br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Precipitation_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
      <GroundOverlay>
        <name>🌧️ LIVE PRECIPITATION</name>
        <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
        <Icon>
          <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/precipitation_na/current.png?v=na-precip-20261013-1535</href>
          <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
          <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
        </Icon>
        <LatLonBox>
          <north>85.0</north>
          <south>5.0</south>
          <east>-15.0</east>
          <west>-180.0</west>
        </LatLonBox>
      </GroundOverlay>
    </Folder>
  </Document>
</kml>
